<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!-- Framework, nullability and analyser settings live in Directory.Build.props. -->

  <!--
    The fifth runtime project. adr/0039: the artefacts that spell things in words — the Input Log
    codec and, from task 8, the crash artifact that wraps it.

    It references Borough.Core and is referenced by both shells, which may never parse or emit a log
    themselves. It does NOT own the save: 05 §7 makes a save an array dump generated from the field
    declaration, and the declaration is in the core, so the save serialiser stays where the thing it
    is generated from lives. The line that keeps this project a boundary rather than a bag is
    *does a human read the tokens*.

    Borough.Analysers is deliberately absent. This project's whole job is to write strings a human
    reads, which is the thing lint 7 forbids in the core — pointing the core's analysers at it would
    fail the build for doing what it exists to do.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Borough.Core\Borough.Core.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <!--
    The Ruleset parser. adr/0048 names it, and names it here rather than in Borough.Core: adr/0003
    requires any *core* dependency be argued explicitly, and this is not one. What protects
    determinism is that the core cannot name this package at all — BoundaryTests asserts it — plus
    the narrower rule the ADR states, that nothing but integers and strings crosses from the parser
    into the loader.

    Chosen on source spans rather than on popularity. adr/0015 promises a refusal names "a file, a
    line, and a rule name", and a syntax tree carrying spans is what makes the third of those
    possible. RulesetLoader therefore walks the tree rather than the model — the model would be
    shorter and would throw every span away.

    adr/0018 demands a written exception naming a property no library provides before anything is
    built by hand. There is no such property here, so writing a TOML parser is not available.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Tomlyn" Version="2.10.1" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
